Subject: [PATCH] bridger: retain hardware activity when refreshing the FDB

Advance the software idle counter before querying hardware statistics. A
recent hardware last-use timestamp can then reset idle to zero even when
the driver has no packet counters. Incrementing idle after the query
prevents FDB refresh for these active flows.

Also skip the rest of the iteration after deleting an idle flow, avoiding
a read from the freed flow.

---
--- a/flow.c
+++ b/flow.c
@@ -198,6 +198,7 @@
 	}
 
 	avl_for_each_element_safe(&flows, flow, node, tmp) {
+		flow->idle++;
 		avl_delete(&sorted_flows, &flow->sort_node);
 		bridger_bpf_flow_update(flow);
 		bridger_nl_flow_offload_update(flow);
@@ -207,8 +208,10 @@
 
 		if (flow->cur_packets)
 			flow->idle = 0;
-		else if (++flow->idle >= 30)
+		else if (flow->idle >= 30) {
 			bridger_flow_delete(flow);
+			continue;
+		}
 
 		if (flow->idle)
 			continue;
